{
  "_doc": "The webcore skin's icon set: every glyph of icons.json (plus the desktop's power / search / more-vertical, the header `logo` mark and the two draw-mode faces) as a 16×16 map of palette characters, `.` transparent, drawn the way the Windows-95 shell drew its own: a black `k` outline round a flat fill, a white or pastel highlight along the top-left inner edge and the fill's darker half-tone along the bottom-right. `i` is ink — a pure symbol's own black (arrows, plus, minus, a frame) — and the one character the dark face re-inks light; `k` stays black on both faces, as the shell's outlines did. The browser (ui/webcore/icons.js) and the desktop (support/webcore/icons.cpp) turn a map into one <rect> per lit run on a 0 0 16 16 viewBox, crisp-edged. `paletteDark` re-inks a character on the dark face — the ink, and every hue too dark to read on it; a character it leaves out keeps its own colour. `logoFrame` is the `logo` mark's ring, which takes the accent as the app's own mark's frame does.",
